    "title": "Where to watch Alabama vs Hofstra today: NCAA Tournament Time, TV info",
    "text": "Updated March 20, 2026, 10:30 p.m. ETIt's officially March Madness for coach Nate Oats' Alabama Crimson Tide. The No. 4 seed faces the No. 13 Hofstra Pride in the first round of the NCAA Tournament's Midwest Region at Benchmark Stadium in Tampa, Florida, on Friday.The Crimson Tide (23-9) ranked 18th in this week's USA TODAY Sports Coaches Poll and AP Top 25 poll. They enter the NCAA Tournament as the top scoring offense in the country, averaging 91.7 points per game. Labaron Philon leads Alabama in scoring; he averages 21.7 points per game. Alabama finished 13-5 in SEC play but is coming off an 80-79 upset loss to Ole Miss at the SEC Tournament in Nashville.Hofstra (24-10) is making its first NCAA Tournament appearance since 2001 after defeating Monmouth, 75-69, to win the Colonial Athletic Association conference title. Cruz Davis leads the Pride in scoring: 20.2 points per game. Preston Edmead averages 16 PPG. Alabama and Hofstra are meeting for the first time in series history.Stream Alabama vs. HofstraWhat channel is Alabama vs. Hofstra on today?TV Channel: truTVLivestream:Watch on SlingAlabama vs. Hofstra will be televised nationally on truTV at the 2026 NCAA Tournament. Tom McCarthy, Candace Parker and Dan Bonner will call the game from Benchmark International Arena, with AJ Ross reporting from the sidelines. Streaming options for the game include Sling.Alabama vs. Hofstra start time today at NCAA TournamentDate: Friday, March 20Start time: 2:15 p.m. CTThe Alabama-Hofstra game starts at 2:15 p.m. CT from Benchmark International Arena in Tampa, Florida.Stream Alabama vs. HofstraAlabama vs. Hofstra basketball game oddsOdds courtesy of BetMGM, updated March 20, 5 a.m. CT.Spread: Alabama by 11 1/2Over/Under: 157 1/2Money line: Alabama (-750), Hofstra (+525)Alabama basketball 2025-26 schedule, resultsNov. 3: vs. North Dakota (W, 91-62)Nov. 8: at St. John's (W, 103-96)Nov. 13: vs. Purdue (L, 87-80)Nov. 19: vs. Illinois (W, 90-86)Nov. 24: vs. Gonzaga (L, 